%%report service-contract-by-status title: Service Contracts by status entity: ServiceContract chart: pie x: status y: records help: A commercial agreement defining purchased support dates, value, renewal, and the entitlements available to an account. How service contracts divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_service_contract WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report service-contract-annual-value-by-status title: Total annual value by status entity: ServiceContract chart: bar x: status y: total_annual_value help: A commercial agreement defining purchased support dates, value, renewal, and the entitlements available to an account. Service Contracts added up on annual value, split by status, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, ROUND(SUM(annual_value)::numeric, 2) AS total_annual_value FROM bus_service_contract WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report service-contract-annual-value-per-month title: Average annual value per month entity: ServiceContract chart: line x: month y: average_annual_value help: A commercial agreement defining purchased support dates, value, renewal, and the entitlements available to an account. The average annual value of service contracts created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(annual_value)::numeric, 2) AS average_annual_value FROM bus_service_contract WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report entitlement-by-status title: Entitlements by status entity: Entitlement chart: pie x: status y: records help: A customer-specific right to receive a defined level and quantity of support under a contract or exception. How entitlements divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_entitlement WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
