%%report case-by-status title: Cases by status entity: Case chart: bar x: status y: records help: The central customer-service request that coordinates ownership, communications, SLA clocks, knowledge, incidents, field work, and resolution. How cases divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_case WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report case-by-priority title: Cases by priority entity: Case chart: pie x: priority y: records help: The central customer-service request that coordinates ownership, communications, SLA clocks, knowledge, incidents, field work, and resolution. How cases divide across priority, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(priority::text, '(unset)') AS priority, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_case WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report case-lifecycle title: Case lifecycle entity: Case chart: bar x: state y: records help: The central customer-service request that coordinates ownership, communications, SLA clocks, knowledge, incidents, field work, and resolution. Where cases sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'new' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'assigned', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'in_progress', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'waiting_customer', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'waiting_internal', 4 UNION ALL SELECT 'resolved', 5 UNION ALL SELECT 'closed', 6 UNION ALL SELECT 'reopened', 7 UNION ALL SELECT 'cancelled', 8) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_case WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report case-comment-created-per-month title: Case Comments created per month entity: CaseComment chart: line x: month y: records help: A timestamped internal or customer-visible update forming the durable working history of a case. New case comments per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_case_comment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report case-comment-public-share title: Case Comments: public entity: CaseComment chart: pie x: public y: records help: A timestamped internal or customer-visible update forming the durable working history of a case. The share of case comments where public holds against those where it does not. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN public THEN 'yes' ELSE 'no' END AS public, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_case_comment WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report case-comment-per-case title: Case Comments per case entity: CaseComment chart: bar x: case y: records help: A timestamped internal or customer-visible update forming the durable working history of a case. Which case the most case comments belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS case, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_case_comment x LEFT JOIN bus_case p ON p.id = x.case_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
