%%report knowledge-article-by-status title: Knowledge Articles by status entity: KnowledgeArticle chart: pie x: status y: records help: A governed support answer or procedure that agents, bots, and customers can discover and reuse. How knowledge articles divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_knowledge_article WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report knowledge-article-by-article-type title: Knowledge Articles by article type entity: KnowledgeArticle chart: pie x: article_type y: records help: A governed support answer or procedure that agents, bots, and customers can discover and reuse. How knowledge articles divide across article type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(article_type::text, '(unset)') AS article_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_knowledge_article WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report knowledge-article-lifecycle title: Knowledge Article lifecycle entity: KnowledgeArticle chart: bar x: state y: records help: A governed support answer or procedure that agents, bots, and customers can discover and reuse. Where knowledge articles sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'draft' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'review', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'approved', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'rejected', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'published', 4 UNION ALL SELECT 'retired', 5) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_knowledge_article WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report knowledge-version-created-per-month title: Knowledge Versions created per month entity: KnowledgeVersion chart: line x: month y: records help: An immutable language-specific revision of a knowledge article retained for approval, publication, rollback, and audit. New knowledge versions per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_knowledge_version WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report knowledge-version-age-bands title: How recently knowledge versions were changed entity: KnowledgeVersion chart: bar x: last_changed y: records help: An immutable language-specific revision of a knowledge article retained for approval, publication, rollback, and audit. Records by time since their last change; the oldest band is the stale tail to review or retire. sql: SELECT CASE WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '30 days' THEN 'last 30 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '90 days' THEN '30 to 90 days' WHEN updated_at >= now() - interval '180 days' THEN '90 to 180 days' ELSE 'older than 180 days' END AS last_changed, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_knowledge_version WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY MIN(updated_at) DESC
%%report knowledge-version-per-knowledge-article title: Knowledge Versions per knowledge article entity: KnowledgeVersion chart: bar x: knowledge_article y: records help: An immutable language-specific revision of a knowledge article retained for approval, publication, rollback, and audit. Which knowledge article the most knowledge versions belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS knowledge_article, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_knowledge_version x LEFT JOIN bus_knowledge_article p ON p.id = x.knowledge_article_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report incident-by-status title: Incidents by status entity: Incident chart: bar x: status y: records help: A service disruption managed across many customer cases with command, restoration, communications, and post-incident review. How incidents divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_incident WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report incident-by-severity title: Incidents by severity entity: Incident chart: pie x: severity y: records help: A service disruption managed across many customer cases with command, restoration, communications, and post-incident review. How incidents divide across severity, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(severity::text, '(unset)') AS severity, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_incident WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report incident-lifecycle title: Incident lifecycle entity: Incident chart: bar x: state y: records help: A service disruption managed across many customer cases with command, restoration, communications, and post-incident review. Where incidents sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'detected' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'triaged', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'investigating', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'mitigating', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'monitoring', 4 UNION ALL SELECT 'restored', 5 UNION ALL SELECT 'review', 6 UNION ALL SELECT 'closed', 7) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_incident WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report problem-by-status title: Problems by status entity: Problem chart: pie x: status y: records help: A recurring or significant underlying cause investigated beyond individual incidents and documented with workarounds and permanent fixes. How problems divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_problem WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report problem-by-priority title: Problems by priority entity: Problem chart: pie x: priority y: records help: A recurring or significant underlying cause investigated beyond individual incidents and documented with workarounds and permanent fixes. How problems divide across priority, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(priority::text, '(unset)') AS priority, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_problem WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report problem-created-per-month title: Problems created per month entity: Problem chart: line x: month y: records help: A recurring or significant underlying cause investigated beyond individual incidents and documented with workarounds and permanent fixes. New problems per month over two years - the volume the business actually handles. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_problem WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report change-request-by-status title: Change Requests by status entity: ChangeRequest chart: bar x: status y: records help: A controlled production modification with risk, approvals, implementation evidence, validation, and a tested rollback plan. How change requests divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_change_request WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report change-request-by-change-type title: Change Requests by change type entity: ChangeRequest chart: pie x: change_type y: records help: A controlled production modification with risk, approvals, implementation evidence, validation, and a tested rollback plan. How change requests divide across change type, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(change_type::text, '(unset)') AS change_type, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_change_request WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report change-request-lifecycle title: Change Request lifecycle entity: ChangeRequest chart: bar x: state y: records help: A controlled production modification with risk, approvals, implementation evidence, validation, and a tested rollback plan. Where change requests sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'draft' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'assessment', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'approval', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'scheduled', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'implementing', 4 UNION ALL SELECT 'validating', 5 UNION ALL SELECT 'completed', 6 UNION ALL SELECT 'failed', 7 UNION ALL SELECT 'rolled_back', 8 UNION ALL SELECT 'cancelled', 9) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_change_request WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
