%%report product-request-by-status title: Product Requests by status entity: ProductRequest chart: bar x: status y: records help: A controlled request to reserve, transfer, ship, or replenish parts needed for service work. How product requests divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_product_request WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report product-request-by-priority title: Product Requests by priority entity: ProductRequest chart: pie x: priority y: records help: A controlled request to reserve, transfer, ship, or replenish parts needed for service work. How product requests divide across priority, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(priority::text, '(unset)') AS priority, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_product_request WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report product-request-lifecycle title: Product Request lifecycle entity: ProductRequest chart: bar x: state y: records help: A controlled request to reserve, transfer, ship, or replenish parts needed for service work. Where product requests sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'draft' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'submitted', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'approved', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'reserved', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'partially_fulfilled', 4 UNION ALL SELECT 'fulfilled', 5 UNION ALL SELECT 'cancelled', 6) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_product_request WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report product-request-line-requested-quantity-per-month title: Average requested quantity per month entity: ProductRequestLine chart: line x: month y: average_requested_quantity help: A requested service part and quantity inside a product request, including partial fulfilment. The average requested quantity of product request lines created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(requested_quantity)::numeric, 2) AS average_requested_quantity FROM bus_product_request_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report product-request-line-fulfilled-quantity-per-month title: Average fulfilled quantity per month entity: ProductRequestLine chart: line x: month y: average_fulfilled_quantity help: A requested service part and quantity inside a product request, including partial fulfilment. The average fulfilled quantity of product request lines created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(fulfilled_quantity)::numeric, 2) AS average_fulfilled_quantity FROM bus_product_request_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report product-request-line-per-product-request title: Product Request Lines per product request entity: ProductRequestLine chart: bar x: product_request y: records help: A requested service part and quantity inside a product request, including partial fulfilment. Which product request the most product request lines belong to; the head of the list is the concentration to know about. sql: SELECT COALESCE(p.name::text, '(none)') AS product_request, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_product_request_line x LEFT JOIN bus_product_request p ON p.id = x.product_request_id AND p.deleted_at IS NULL WHERE x.deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC LIMIT 10
%%report return-order-by-status title: Return Orders by status entity: ReturnOrder chart: bar x: status y: records help: A controlled reverse-logistics transaction for customer equipment, defective parts, loaners, or replacement units. How return orders divide across status, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(status::text, '(unset)') AS status, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_return_order WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report return-order-by-return-reason title: Return Orders by return reason entity: ReturnOrder chart: pie x: return_reason y: records help: A controlled reverse-logistics transaction for customer equipment, defective parts, loaners, or replacement units. How return orders divide across return reason, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(return_reason::text, '(unset)') AS return_reason, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_return_order WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report return-order-lifecycle title: Return Order lifecycle entity: ReturnOrder chart: bar x: state y: records help: A controlled reverse-logistics transaction for customer equipment, defective parts, loaners, or replacement units. Where return orders sit in their state machine, in the order the diagram draws it; a state nothing has reached shows as zero. sql: SELECT d.state, COALESCE(c.records, 0) AS records FROM (SELECT 'requested' AS state, 0 AS position UNION ALL SELECT 'authorised', 1 UNION ALL SELECT 'in_transit', 2 UNION ALL SELECT 'received', 3 UNION ALL SELECT 'inspecting', 4 UNION ALL SELECT 'disposed', 5 UNION ALL SELECT 'closed', 6 UNION ALL SELECT 'cancelled', 7) d LEFT JOIN (SELECT status AS state, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_return_order WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1) c ON c.state = d.state ORDER BY d.position
%%report return-order-line-by-disposition title: Return Order Lines by disposition entity: ReturnOrderLine chart: pie x: disposition y: records help: An authorised item inside a return order with quantity, serial context, inspection, and final disposition. How return order lines divide across disposition, so the dominant group and the empty ones are both visible. sql: SELECT COALESCE(disposition::text, '(unset)') AS disposition, COUNT(*) AS records FROM bus_return_order_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
%%report return-order-line-quantity-by-disposition title: Total quantity by disposition entity: ReturnOrderLine chart: bar x: disposition y: total_quantity help: An authorised item inside a return order with quantity, serial context, inspection, and final disposition. Return Order Lines added up on quantity, split by disposition, to show where the quantity sits. sql: SELECT COALESCE(disposition::text, '(unset)') AS disposition, ROUND(SUM(quantity)::numeric, 2) AS total_quantity FROM bus_return_order_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC NULLS LAST
%%report return-order-line-quantity-per-month title: Average quantity per month entity: ReturnOrderLine chart: line x: month y: average_quantity help: An authorised item inside a return order with quantity, serial context, inspection, and final disposition. The average quantity of return order lines created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(quantity)::numeric, 2) AS average_quantity FROM bus_return_order_line WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report forecast-expected-volume-per-month title: Average expected volume per month entity: Forecast chart: line x: month y: average_expected_volume help: A queue-level workload and staffing prediction used to plan shifts, service levels, and capacity. The average expected volume of forecasts created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(expected_volume)::numeric, 2) AS average_expected_volume FROM bus_forecast WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
%%report forecast-largest-by-expected-volume title: The ten largest forecasts by expected volume entity: Forecast chart: bar x: record y: expected_volume help: A queue-level workload and staffing prediction used to plan shifts, service levels, and capacity. The records with the highest expected volume; worth reading for outliers and for the few that carry most of the total. sql: SELECT name::text AS record, expected_volume FROM bus_forecast WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND expected_volume IS NOT NULL ORDER BY expected_volume DESC LIMIT 10
%%report forecast-expected-handle-minutes-per-month title: Average expected handle minutes per month entity: Forecast chart: line x: month y: average_expected_handle_minutes help: A queue-level workload and staffing prediction used to plan shifts, service levels, and capacity. The average expected handle minutes of forecasts created each month, to see whether the typical record is growing or shrinking. sql: SELECT to_char(date_trunc('month', created_at), 'YYYY-MM') AS month, ROUND(AVG(expected_handle_minutes)::numeric, 2) AS average_expected_handle_minutes FROM bus_forecast WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND created_at >= now() - interval '24 months' GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1
